ce text, including headings such as **“CHAPTER-2”**, **“SECTION-1”**, and repeated bases such as A, C, G, and T arranged in lines.\n\nPanel **B** shows another document page with mixed, partly distorted text. It includes visible headings such as **“CHAPTER-2”** and **“SECTION-1”**, with words resembling biological/sequence-related labels, but the text is degraded and not fully legible.\n\nVisible biological source objects: nucleotide/DNA sequence text in panel A.  \nVisible transformations/model interfaces: document viewer/PDF interface screenshots; panel B appears to show corrupted or transformed text relative to normal readable sequence/document text.  \nFindings: the figure visually compares readable biological sequence/document content with a degraded or altered text output, but the exact method or conclusion cannot be determined from the image alone."]}]

